1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Fire has no 'up' in space.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
The Moon base will likely use 30% oxygen or more, where fire is harder to predict.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:21,000
NASA's fire data stops at orbit. FlameSense shows where it ends, predicts only where data exists, and ranks the experiments NASA should run next.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Built on NASA's ISS combustion data: BASS, BASS-II and Saffire.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Open source, live now.
